# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF on
# every platform.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a
# Windows checkout receives a CRLF copy of every source file and
# `prettier --check`, whose `endOfLine` default is `lf`, fails on files that are
# correct everywhere else. Cost Guard is developed on Windows, so this matters
# on the first clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
